## english FAQ
English FAQ: ❓
- Q: What is PELITA? A: A web-based educational health game.
- Q: Who made PELITA? A: Fauzan, a junior high school student.
- Q: Is it free? A: Yes, 100% free.
- Q: How to play? A: Read story, choose answer, get feedback.
- Q: How long? A: 20-30 minutes.
- Q: Platform? A: Web browser (HP or computer).
- Q: Language? A: Indonesian.
- Q: Age? A: 13-17 years old.

## english about the creator
About the creator (English): 🧑‍💻
"PELITA was created by Fauzan (Muhamad Fauzan Riyadi Irham), a junior high school student at SMP Muhammadiyah 17 Ciputat. He developed the game independently, handling coding, design, and content. He was mentored by Ms. Okta, a ICT teacher. PELITA is his entry for LKIP XIII 2026 in the field of Information Technology, Computing, and Digital Innovation."

## english about the game
About the game (English): 🎮
"PELITA features 12 chapters, each representing one WHO health literacy indicator. Players read a story, choose one of three answers, and receive immediate feedback. Correct answers earn a star; wrong answers provide educational explanations. The game uses 'Cinema Mode' (dark background) for focus and applies positive reinforcement (no punishment)."

## english about the research
About the research (English): 🔬
"PELITA uses One-Shot Case Study design with post-test and user acceptance survey. 26 students from SMP Muhammadiyah 17 Ciputat participated. Results show average cognitive achievement above 85%, exceeding national vulnerability data. Limitations are acknowledged honestly in the report."

